.TH QBUCKET 1 "2026-10-24" "qbucket 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qbucket \- browser for S3 and S3-compatible object storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qbucket
.RI [ Qt-options ]
.br
.B qbucket
.BR \-\-self\-test " | " \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
QBucket browses and manages buckets and objects on Amazon S3 and
S3-compatible servers such as Hetzner Object Storage, Ceph RGW and Garage.
Every change is planned, previewed, verified and journaled.
Secrets are kept in the system keychain (Secret Service or KWallet); without
one, QBucket asks for them once per session and keeps them in memory only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Check the installation without opening a window: print the version, the Qt
in use, the sandbox, the settings, data and cache paths, and write, read
back and remove a test entry in the keychain.
Exits with 0 when the keychain works, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/qbucket/qbucket/
Settings, accounts (never a secret), bookmarks.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qbucket/qbucket/
Journal, transfer state, server capabilities.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/qbucket/qbucket/
Files opened in other applications and copies staged for dragging out.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/theinvisible/qbucket
